ArrCustomFormatImportRequest.description:
`POST /customformats/import-from-arr`: read CFs + profiles from a live
Sonarr/Radarr. `kind` picks the media_kind (sonarr->series, radarr->movie);
the `url` + `api_key` reach the arr's `/api/v3` surface.

BulkRootResult.description:
Result of `POST /api/v1/library/bulk/root-folder` (tier-scoped verified
move). `affected` = editions whose root was successfully retargeted;
`skipped` = selected items that had no edition of the requested tier;
`errors` = per-edition move failures that did NOT abort the batch.

CommandStatus.description:
Lifecycle state of a :class:`~fusionha.models.command_run.CommandRun`.

``RUNNING`` while the pass is in flight; ``COMPLETED`` on a clean finish;
``INTERRUPTED`` when the process died mid-run (a restart reconciles orphans);
``FAILED`` when the pass raised.

DiscoverIgnoreRead.description:
One Discover ignore row (reversible hide) for the Settings restore surface.

`scope` is `"collection"` (a whole franchise card hidden from the rail;
`tmdb_id` is null) or `"item"` (one film hidden within `collection_tmdb_id`;
`tmdb_id` is the film). `name`/`collection_name` are denormalised labels so
the restore list renders without a live TMDB call.

FourKAvailablePage.description:
Paged "4K Available" feed (#62). ``total`` is the number of TITLE entries;
``fourk_available_count`` is the library-wide count of qualifying titles that
drives the Wanted tab badge (equal to ``total`` -- paging is per-title).

RequestStatus.description:
Lifecycle state of a native :class:`~fusionha.models.requests.MediaRequest`
(P3 Requests & Approvals — the Overseerr-replacement flow for NATIVE-UI users).

* ``PENDING``   — submitted, awaiting an approver's decision;
* ``APPROVED``  — an approver (or an auto-approve policy) accepted it; the
  edition is created + monitored via the shared Add path (still writes the row);
* ``REJECTED``  — declined, with a required :class:`RequestReason` (+ optional note);
* ``DEFERRED``  — a temporary "not available yet"; stays on the requester's
  list with its reason until it can be re-decided;
* ``FULFILLED`` — **DERIVED at read time, NEVER written**: the request's edition
  owns a file ("Available"). The member exists only so the serializer can
  project ``status -> "fulfilled"`` without a stored (and stale-prone) value.
